    "final_answer": "I have found and read the latest Diffusion-related blog on Hugging Face. Here is my summary:\n\n## Latest Diffusion Blog: \"Waypoint-1.5: Higher-Fidelity Interactive Worlds for Everyday GPUs\"\n\n**Published:** April 9, 2026\n**Authors:** Andrew Lapp, Louis Castricato, Scott Fox, Shahbuland Matiana, and David Rossi (the Overworld team)\n**Tags:** Announcement, Diffusion, World-Model\n\n### Intro/Overview Summary (\"What is Waypoint-1.5?\")\n\nThe blog introduces **Waypoint-1.5**, Overworld's next-generation **real-time video world model**, designed to bring interactive generative worlds to hardware that everyday people actually own — not just datacenter-scale compute.\n\nKey points from the intro:\n\n1. **Foundation from the first release:** The original Waypoint demonstrated that real-time generative worlds were possible, proving that interactive world models could go beyond passive video demos and that locally runnable systems could begin to close the gap between *generating* a world and *actually stepping into* one.\n\n2. **Builds on the foundation:** Waypoint-1.5 directly extends that work with three main improvements:\n   - **Higher visual fidelity**\n   - **Expanded hardware range** — the model can now run locally on a wider variety of consumer-grade hardware\n   - **Closer to interactive world simulation** without requiring datacenter-scale compute\n\n3. **Vision:** The team positions Waypoint-1.5 as a meaningful step toward truly interactive world simulation that is accessible to everyday users on everyday GPUs, democratizing real-time generative video world experiences beyond large-scale cloud infrastructure.\n\n### Subsequent Sections (preview)\nThe blog then goes on to detail \"What's new in Waypoint-1.5?\", covering improvements in accessibility, expanded local-run capabilities, scaled training, and additional under-the-hood technical enhancements. It also points to models hosted on the Hub: `Overworld/Waypoint-1.5-1B` and `Overworld/Waypoint-1.5-1B-360P`, with links to try the experience via overworld.stream and the Biome desktop client.",
